1
00:01:47,059 --> 00:01:48,183
Look at that!

2
00:01:48,494 --> 00:01:51,360
All right, good. Now stand
to the right of the tree.

3
00:01:51,719 --> 00:01:52,910
All right, around here?

4
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,454
Yeah, get closer to the tree.

5
00:01:55,048 --> 00:01:56,340
A little more to the left.

6
00:01:58,259 --> 00:01:59,602
Around here?

7
00:02:00,014 --> 00:02:01,691
All right, right there. Good.

8
00:02:01,979 --> 00:02:03,918
Come on, let's wrap this up quickly.

9
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:06,600
What on earth are they doing?

10
00:02:07,274 --> 00:02:09,364
They seem to be peering through something.

11
00:02:09,388 --> 00:02:11,035
What can you see, Mr. Screech Owl?

12
00:02:11,849 --> 00:02:15,640
Oh, I can't see a thing until nightfall.

13
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:18,660
I've got a bad feeling about this.

14
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:22,377
Listen, my babies are about to be
born. What if something happens?

15
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:26,092
I've seen that before.
They're surveying the land.

16
00:02:26,910 --> 00:02:29,200
What do they plan on
doing once it's surveyed?

17
00:02:29,385 --> 00:02:30,385
Beats me!

18
00:02:35,383 --> 00:02:37,271
That really is a massive tree.

19
00:02:38,339 --> 00:02:39,805
You're so right, Boss.

20
00:02:40,836 --> 00:02:42,316
That tree really bothers me.

21
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:43,340
I know!

22
00:02:46,495 --> 00:02:52,437
♪ Koorogi-ko wa boku no tomodachi. ♪
The little cricket is my friend.

23
00:02:52,875 --> 00:02:57,974
♪ Tottemo suteki na nakayoshi nano sa. ♪
We're the very best of pals.

24
00:02:57,999 --> 00:02:59,089
- Mokkun umai na~
Mokku sure is good at this!

25
00:02:59,114 --> 00:03:00,579
♪ Dakedo dake... ♪
But... bu...

26
00:03:00,603 --> 00:03:02,220
Hey Mokku!

27
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:05,659
Hey, Giorgio, good morning!

28
00:03:05,739 --> 00:03:08,103
Mokku, could you come here for a second?

29
00:03:08,225 --> 00:03:12,880
No way, I'm heading to school.
I don't have time to dilly-dally.

30
00:03:13,215 --> 00:03:17,215
I know, but it won't take long. Please!

31
00:03:17,555 --> 00:03:22,039
I have to be a good boy if I want
to become human. Don't tempt me.

32
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,855
It's hard enough for me
to stay on track as it is.

33
00:03:25,134 --> 00:03:27,976
Some human adults
gathered around the Oak Tree...

34
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,945
...and they're doing something strange.

35
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:33,040
What? Around the Oak Tree?

36
00:03:33,576 --> 00:03:37,198
I have a bad feeling something
awful is about to happen.

37
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:40,480
What on earth are they trying to do?

38
00:03:40,804 --> 00:03:42,860
Please, go find out what's going on.

39
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:45,604
I can't understand human speech.

40
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:48,860
You say you've got a bad feeling?

41
00:03:49,269 --> 00:03:50,320
All right, I'll go.

42
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:52,280
Thanks, Mokku. Let's go!

43
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,212
All right!

44
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:55,260
Mokku...

45
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:03,620
Mokku is actually trying to do
something to help Giorgio today.

46
00:04:03,984 --> 00:04:07,446
Well, I won't scold him for straying this
time. Let's just see how this plays out.

47
00:04:11,024 --> 00:04:13,570
Huh? Aren't they just surveying the land?

48
00:04:14,119 --> 00:04:16,399
The one setting up the
pole is Franco's papa.

49
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,459
I know that.

50
00:04:18,725 --> 00:04:22,588
You want to know what on
earth they're doing that for, right?

51
00:04:22,612 --> 00:04:24,595
Got it. I'll go ask for you.

52
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,872
Franco's papa, good morning!

53
00:04:32,260 --> 00:04:34,083
Franco's papa!

54
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:35,170
What?

55
00:04:35,925 --> 00:04:37,338
Oh, it's Mokku.

56
00:04:37,362 --> 00:04:39,313
What are you measuring this place for?

57
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,160
What's this?

58
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:43,231
Hey! What are you peeking at?!

59
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,635
This isn't for kids to see!

60
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:50,096
Fix my neck, my neck!

61
00:04:50,394 --> 00:04:52,780
Boss, shall we head down the mountain soon?

62
00:04:56,542 --> 00:04:58,542
That was awful...

63
00:04:59,810 --> 00:05:01,123
Huh, they left.

64
00:05:04,910 --> 00:05:06,980
Hey, Mokku. Did you find out?

65
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:08,658
No, no good.

66
00:05:08,925 --> 00:05:10,940
And you were our only hope.

67
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,740
Aw, don't look so sad.

68
00:05:14,265 --> 00:05:16,885
I know, I'll ask Franco. All right?

69
00:05:20,935 --> 00:05:22,329
Is that true, Franco?

70
00:05:22,828 --> 00:05:23,910
Yeah, it's true.

71
00:05:24,165 --> 00:05:26,484
I heard Papa talking to
Mama about it last night.

72
00:05:26,905 --> 00:05:29,390
It's gonna be great once
the amusement park is built!

73
00:05:29,990 --> 00:05:33,543
But Franco, what on earth
is an amusement park?

74
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:35,860
It's a playground for kids like us.

75
00:05:36,125 --> 00:05:39,279
They're building an amusement
park with all kinds of rides.

76
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:41,205
It's gonna be amazing!

77
00:05:41,230 --> 00:05:45,863
It's a kids' paradise, with a carousel,
a Ferris wheel, and tons of rides!

78
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:20,660
Wow, that sounds
like it'll be a lot of fun.

79
00:06:21,045 --> 00:06:24,733
Come on, you'll get to play
there every day, so you must
be looking forward to it, too.

80
00:06:25,145 --> 00:06:27,023
Yeah, I hope it's finished soon.

81
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:31,049
Hey, Franco, tell your papa
to hurry up and build it!

82
00:06:31,073 --> 00:06:32,880
Sure, will do. I'll tell him.

83
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:37,120
Franco's papa is really amazing.

84
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:39,260
You bet he is!

85
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:41,980
Huh? An amusement park here?

86
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:45,680
It's the quietest place in
the village, with the best view.

87
00:06:45,930 --> 00:06:49,805
They say they're building a huge
one, with tons of things to play on.

88
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:53,380
But this Oak Tree will be
all right, won't it, Mokku?

89
00:06:55,825 --> 00:06:59,359
That's right. They wouldn't
cut it down, would they?

90
00:06:59,575 --> 00:07:03,760
Well... I didn't ask about that.

91
00:07:04,010 --> 00:07:06,877
What if it gets chopped down?

92
00:07:06,901 --> 00:07:09,980
What will we do? We
won't have anywhere to live!

93
00:07:10,115 --> 00:07:12,640
Mokku, that's not going to happen, right?

94
00:07:12,672 --> 00:07:17,004
D-Don't ask me. It's not
like I'm the one building it.

95
00:07:17,419 --> 00:07:19,719
Mokku, this affects you, too!

96
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:25,660
It's useless if you don't ask the most
important thing! Hurry up and find out!

97
00:07:25,895 --> 00:07:27,346
B-But...

98
00:07:27,370 --> 00:07:31,526
Just go! If you dawdle, I'll
poke your butt like last time!

99
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:32,588
A-All right, I get it!

100
00:07:32,612 --> 00:07:34,520
Mokku, hurry up, hurry!

101
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:36,110
Quit dragging your feet!

102
00:07:36,215 --> 00:07:37,936
I'm going, I'm going!

103
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:40,171
We're counting on you, Mokku!

104
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:44,320
I wonder if Mokku will be okay.
He doesn't seem very reliable.

105
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:49,206
Man, that scared me. Why
does everyone get so worked up?

106
00:07:52,885 --> 00:07:56,495
Ugh, I got dirt in my mouth. Geez.

107
00:07:57,235 --> 00:08:02,188
Why do I have to rush around
like this? Give me a break.

108
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:05,949
Oh no, look what I did.

109
00:08:08,085 --> 00:08:09,800
It has nothing to do with me anyway.

110
00:08:10,367 --> 00:08:12,816
Whether that Oak Tree gets chopped
down or whatever happens to it...

111
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:14,172
...it's not my problem.

112
00:08:14,950 --> 00:08:15,950
You idiot!

113
00:08:15,975 --> 00:08:17,494
You ungrateful brat!

114
00:08:18,010 --> 00:08:20,580
That Oak Tree is your mother!

115
00:08:20,945 --> 00:08:21,945
My mother?

116
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:22,940
Listen to me!

117
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:28,318
The Fairy who gave you life
lives in that Oak Tree! You big fool!

118
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:31,400
The Fairy who gave me life...

119
00:08:37,709 --> 00:08:42,440
Mokku, I am the Fairy of
the Oak Tree, your home.

120
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:49,040
I have heard Grandfather's wish,
and I have come to give you life.

121
00:08:49,975 --> 00:08:52,844
Grant life to the wooden puppet, Mokku.

122
00:09:02,259 --> 00:09:05,642
And Mokku, do you remember...

123
00:09:05,932 --> 00:09:08,205
...when you fell into this stream...

124
00:09:08,229 --> 00:09:10,566
...and were almost smashed
to pieces in the waterfall basin...

125
00:09:10,749 --> 00:09:13,780
Who was it that reached
out a hand to save you?

126
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:20,800
Help me!

127
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,807
Hang in there, Mokku!

128
00:09:39,629 --> 00:09:42,026
Mokku, hold on!

129
00:09:42,929 --> 00:09:43,929
Be brave!

130
00:09:45,569 --> 00:09:48,397
If you give up over something like
this, you can never become human.

131
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:51,125
Now, take heart and climb out.

132
00:09:56,739 --> 00:09:59,620
Do you really not care if that
Oak Tree gets chopped down?

133
00:10:00,860 --> 00:10:05,551
I'll ask Franco's papa to see if they're
really going to cut down the Oak Tree.

134
00:10:05,895 --> 00:10:08,740
That's it, that's the spirit!
I'm counting on you, Mokku.

135
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:11,108
Hey, wait up. I'm coming too.

136
00:10:16,636 --> 00:10:17,840
Cheers!

137
00:10:17,870 --> 00:10:20,118
To celebrate the President's new project...

138
00:10:22,968 --> 00:10:25,884
I made a success of the
coastal tourism business.

139
00:10:25,908 --> 00:10:30,160
This time, I'll make sure that mountain
amusement park succeeds without fail!

140
00:10:31,803 --> 00:10:35,096
Once it's built, huge
crowds will be packing in!

141
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:37,642
Which means money will come rolling in...

142
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:42,010
Yes, I'll do anything for money!

143
00:10:42,316 --> 00:10:45,280
I have to build the amusement
park as soon as possible!

144
00:10:47,019 --> 00:10:52,360
To do that, first we've gotta chop down
that huge oak tree on top of the mountain!

145
00:10:52,384 --> 00:10:53,532
I knew it...

146
00:10:54,244 --> 00:10:57,274
Mokku! They really are going
to cut down the Oak Tree!

147
00:10:57,298 --> 00:10:58,949
Are you just going to let them, Mokku?!

148
00:11:00,014 --> 00:11:03,920
The Oak Tree... The Oak Tree 
is going to be cut down...

149
00:11:09,328 --> 00:11:10,335
Stop!

150
00:11:11,025 --> 00:11:12,204
Help!

151
00:11:16,279 --> 00:11:19,246
Stop! Stop!

152
00:11:33,856 --> 00:11:36,189
Please stop!

153
00:11:39,089 --> 00:11:41,392
Mokku, help me!

154
00:11:41,889 --> 00:11:44,800
Stop it! Please stop!

155
00:12:08,209 --> 00:12:11,137
A dream...? Thank goodness
it was just a dream...

156
00:12:24,419 --> 00:12:28,680
All right! I'll definitely
protect that Oak Tree!

157
00:12:31,789 --> 00:12:34,976
♪ Ore wa kono mura no nanushi ♪
I'm the headman of this village—

158
00:12:35,001 --> 00:12:37,288
♪ Shiruku Hato ni mo ♪
...and to think even Silk Hat...

159
00:12:37,313 --> 00:12:39,649
♪ nigete kuru ka to. ♪
...comes running to me!

160
00:12:39,905 --> 00:12:41,419
♪ Etto ♪
Uh, so...

161
00:12:41,443 --> 00:12:43,269
♪ ojiji-sama no okaeri da to. ♪
...the old master's coming home, is he?

162
00:12:43,294 --> 00:12:44,339
Franco's papa!

163
00:12:46,051 --> 00:12:47,200
Who is it?

164
00:12:49,863 --> 00:12:50,972
Sorry...

165
00:12:51,519 --> 00:12:54,118
There are two or three of you.

166
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:57,260
What is it? What do you want?

167
00:12:57,359 --> 00:13:00,720
Is it true they're building an amusement
park on the Oak Tree's mountain?

168
00:13:01,055 --> 00:13:04,300
Yeah, that's right. And it's
going to be something incredible.

169
00:13:04,688 --> 00:13:06,057
Could you please stop?

170
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:09,172
Huh? Yeah, sure, like I'd stop!

171
00:13:09,370 --> 00:13:10,615
Wh-What?

172
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:12,625
That Oak Tree on my hill...

173
00:13:12,649 --> 00:13:16,580
I mean, all kinds of animals
and insects live in that tree.

174
00:13:17,124 --> 00:13:19,725
So please, can't you
leave it the way it is?

175
00:13:20,275 --> 00:13:21,983
Stop messing around!

176
00:13:22,609 --> 00:13:25,109
What kind of nonsense
are you talking? Shut up!

177
00:13:25,165 --> 00:13:26,420
Give your stupidity a rest!

178
00:13:26,421 --> 00:13:28,060
Please. Stop it.

179
00:13:28,745 --> 00:13:29,944
Shut up!

180
00:13:30,014 --> 00:13:31,980
Please, listen to me! I'm begging you!

181
00:13:32,392 --> 00:13:33,776
Like hell we'll listen to that!

182
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,990
Ah! Mokku!

183
00:13:38,290 --> 00:13:39,800
Oh, that's terrible.

184
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:41,300
Mokku, are you all right?

185
00:13:41,530 --> 00:13:43,290
Spouting such nonsense.

186
00:13:45,109 --> 00:13:47,016
Come on, Mokku, pull yourself together!

187
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,760
Oh, no, I can't go to school like this.

188
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:52,555
What a cruel thing to do.

189
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:55,520
Now, if you've learned your
lesson, hurry up and go home.

190
00:13:58,292 --> 00:13:59,047
Giorgio!

191
00:13:59,861 --> 00:14:00,995
Eh! Hey!

192
00:14:03,656 --> 00:14:05,570
Hey! Give my hat back!

193
00:14:05,665 --> 00:14:08,140
You little prankster, 
get down from there right now!

194
00:14:11,422 --> 00:14:13,293
Serves you right!

195
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:16,280
Making a fool out of me... 
just watch what I'll do!

196
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,200
Ah, a gun!

197
00:14:22,659 --> 00:14:24,034
Oh! So feisty!

198
00:14:24,058 --> 00:14:26,191
How exciting!

199
00:14:32,695 --> 00:14:33,753
Look out Giorgio!

200
00:14:34,496 --> 00:14:35,857
Stop! Stop!

201
00:14:36,562 --> 00:14:37,320
Shut up!

202
00:14:42,229 --> 00:14:43,229
My hand...

203
00:14:44,509 --> 00:14:46,124
It snapped...

204
00:14:55,966 --> 00:14:56,966
Giorgio!

205
00:14:57,742 --> 00:14:58,742
Giorgio!

206
00:14:59,890 --> 00:15:00,890
Hang in there!

207
00:15:04,629 --> 00:15:05,920
Serves you right!

208
00:15:11,139 --> 00:15:14,516
Grandpa, Giorgio will be
able to fly again, won't he?

209
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:19,620
The injury isn't serious. He'll
heal if he rests for a day or two.

210
00:15:20,179 --> 00:15:21,320
That's a relief, Giorgio.

211
00:15:21,745 --> 00:15:26,720
If the Oak Tree is going to be chopped
down, who cares if my wings heal or not.

212
00:15:27,829 --> 00:15:29,440
What are you saying, Giorgio?

213
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:33,960
Because it's true! Everyone's
home will be gone!

214
00:15:35,249 --> 00:15:37,500
There's no point in living like that.

215
00:15:38,405 --> 00:15:41,600
Now then, Mokku's hand... let's see.

216
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:44,721
Oh, that's right. I used up
the rest of the oak wood...

217
00:15:44,745 --> 00:15:47,980
...when I fixed Mokku's leg the other day.

218
00:15:50,555 --> 00:15:55,000
Don't worry anymore. I'll
go negotiate with Vittorio.

219
00:15:55,275 --> 00:15:57,070
Really, Grandpa?!

220
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:04,340
The plateau with that Oak Tree has
the most beautiful view in the village.

221
00:16:04,735 --> 00:16:09,280
I am completely against building some
gaudy playground in a place like that.

222
00:16:09,855 --> 00:16:12,820
The sensible villagers
will surely oppose it too.

223
00:16:13,530 --> 00:16:16,260
We'll all stand together
and protect the Oak Tree.

224
00:16:16,805 --> 00:16:18,060
Please do, Grandpa.

225
00:16:18,609 --> 00:16:20,500
Isn't that great, Giorgio?

226
00:16:20,665 --> 00:16:24,820
Yeah. I want to go tell the
squirrels and wild birds right away.

227
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:27,640
Mokku, look, your arm is all finished.

228
00:16:28,425 --> 00:16:32,569
Being a wooden puppet makes you easy
to repair, thankfully. There, how's that?

229
00:16:33,110 --> 00:16:34,238
Thank you, Grandpa.

230
00:16:35,209 --> 00:16:37,317
Huh, that's weird.

231
00:16:40,109 --> 00:16:41,240
What's wrong with it?

232
00:16:43,359 --> 00:16:45,026
Hm? What's the matter?

233
00:16:46,089 --> 00:16:48,980
Grandpa, it won't move like it used to.

234
00:16:49,237 --> 00:16:52,108
It isn't from the Oak Tree, so it
probably won't move right away.

235
00:16:52,133 --> 00:16:54,302
Don't worry, it'll move
once you get used to it.

236
00:16:54,725 --> 00:16:56,980
Well, I have to go talk to him.

237
00:16:58,180 --> 00:16:59,265
I wonder...

238
00:17:02,689 --> 00:17:04,015
What the hell are you babbling about?

239
00:17:04,156 --> 00:17:06,229
An old geezer like you
has no business interfering!

240
00:17:06,589 --> 00:17:09,980
Vittorio, please. This is a peaceful
mountain. I want you to leave it in peace.

241
00:17:10,244 --> 00:17:13,760
The mountain is far more beautiful as
it is than with some amusement park.

242
00:17:13,784 --> 00:17:16,101
You just stick to your
woodcarving, old man!

243
00:17:16,281 --> 00:17:20,060
Building an amusement park there
is already a done deal. Now get lost!

244
00:17:20,904 --> 00:17:23,275
No matter how much you object,
it won't change a thing, old man!

245
00:17:23,713 --> 00:17:25,642
B-But, Vittorio!

246
00:17:25,730 --> 00:17:26,629
Goodbye!

247
00:17:33,312 --> 00:17:35,300
Then there's really no
saving the Oak Tree...

248
00:17:35,715 --> 00:17:39,102
Forgive me, it's all
because I'm so powerless.

249
00:17:39,337 --> 00:17:42,680
Let us pray to God to
protect the Oak Tree...

250
00:17:42,979 --> 00:17:45,974
That's the only thing we can do right now.

251
00:17:52,199 --> 00:17:57,960
God, please protect the Oak
Tree. Please hear Mokku's prayer.

252
00:18:17,099 --> 00:18:19,780
Hurry up and get ready!
Do you have all the tools?

253
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:21,180
Yes!

254
00:18:25,139 --> 00:18:27,725
All right, let's begin! Cut that tree down!

255
00:18:31,414 --> 00:18:32,769
Ah, at last...

256
00:18:32,793 --> 00:18:34,656
...our final moment come...

257
00:18:36,513 --> 00:18:38,287
All right, let's do this...

258
00:18:43,558 --> 00:18:44,653
Hey!

259
00:18:44,834 --> 00:18:46,255
Ah! It's Mokku!

260
00:18:46,939 --> 00:18:49,739
Stop it! Stop cutting down the Oak Tree!

261
00:18:49,912 --> 00:18:51,718
This is none of your business!

262
00:18:54,266 --> 00:18:56,542
Stop! Please, I'm begging you!

263
00:18:56,956 --> 00:18:58,065
Get lost!

264
00:18:59,259 --> 00:19:02,440
Keep getting in our way and
I'll smash you to pieces first!

265
00:19:03,124 --> 00:19:05,800
Hey! Wait! Stop! I beg of you!

266
00:19:05,801 --> 00:19:09,210
Listen here, old man! Get in our
way again and you won't be spared!

267
00:19:09,429 --> 00:19:13,696
That's right, I have official
permission from the town hall!

268
00:19:14,619 --> 00:19:19,390
Grandpa, if they cut down
the Oak Tree, I'd rather die!

269
00:19:19,809 --> 00:19:21,735
All right, boys, get to it!

270
00:19:24,614 --> 00:19:26,498
Mokku, what are you saying?

271
00:19:26,552 --> 00:19:30,412
But Grandpa, Mama... the Oak
Tree is going to be cut down!

272
00:19:30,584 --> 00:19:33,860
Mokku, pray. Pray to God.

273
00:19:35,486 --> 00:19:37,206
What are you muttering...?

274
00:19:37,824 --> 00:19:41,551
God! Please! Please save the Oak Tree!

275
00:19:41,876 --> 00:19:45,280
Please save the Oak Tree... Save my mother!

276
00:19:45,824 --> 00:19:49,325
I beg you! Take my life instead!

277
00:19:50,379 --> 00:19:54,220
Please... Please save my mother!

278
00:19:55,125 --> 00:19:56,125
God!

279
00:19:56,779 --> 00:19:58,449
All right, let's do this!

280
00:20:01,024 --> 00:20:02,747
God!

281
00:20:18,159 --> 00:20:19,600
Divine punishment from the oak tree!

282
00:20:19,620 --> 00:20:20,780
The oak tree is cursed!

283
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:23,800


284
00:20:30,516 --> 00:20:31,316
Help!

285
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:33,020
Forget it!

286
00:20:33,948 --> 00:20:35,400
Run!

287
00:20:38,987 --> 00:20:40,390
Help!

288
00:20:41,789 --> 00:20:42,789
Grandpa!

289
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:44,255
Mokku!

290
00:20:46,685 --> 00:20:49,068
Help me!

291
00:20:53,379 --> 00:20:54,762
Help me!

292
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:57,539
Somebody help me!

293
00:20:57,784 --> 00:21:00,260
Help me!

294
00:21:00,349 --> 00:21:02,660
Vittorio, take my hand!

295
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:05,580
Grandpa, you shouldn't help a guy like him!

296
00:21:06,292 --> 00:21:07,292
Fool!

297
00:21:08,719 --> 00:21:10,300
Come on, grab on, Vittorio!

298
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:13,047
I-I'm sorry...

299
00:21:29,109 --> 00:21:31,260
Hold on, Mokku. Almost there.

300
00:21:39,624 --> 00:21:42,677
Thank you, Mokku. Thank you.

301
00:21:45,649 --> 00:21:48,049
I'm sorry. Please forgive me.

302
00:21:49,974 --> 00:21:53,180
You did well, Mokku.
Everything is all right now.

303
00:21:56,859 --> 00:21:59,180
Thank goodness! I'm so glad!

304
00:21:59,304 --> 00:22:00,820
It's all thanks to Mokku!

305
00:22:23,939 --> 00:22:26,780
Mokku, you did so well
protecting the Oak Tree.

306
00:22:27,219 --> 00:22:31,860
Thank you. And you did well to
help others with that disabled hand.

307
00:22:33,681 --> 00:22:35,539
I will give you a reward.

308
00:22:36,165 --> 00:22:40,806
I shall transfer the life of the oak
branch struck by lightning into this hand.

309
00:22:51,154 --> 00:22:53,903
Ah! It moves! It's moving!

310
00:22:54,529 --> 00:22:59,710
Grandpa! Grandpa! I-I-It's
fixed! My left hand can move!

311
00:23:00,359 --> 00:23:02,564
Is that so? That's wonderful!

312
00:23:02,855 --> 00:23:06,731
The Fairy was right after
all! It moves, Grandpa!

313
00:23:07,776 --> 00:23:12,580
Because you tried so hard to protect
the Oak Tree, God healed it for you.

314
00:23:14,499 --> 00:23:18,160
If only you were always a good boy like
this, I wouldn't have such a hard time.

315
00:23:19,569 --> 00:23:22,151
Mokku is gradually becoming a good boy.

316
00:23:33,569 --> 00:23:36,887
<i>Learning that Mokku is at his wit's
end after insects ate one of his legs...</i>

317
00:23:36,911 --> 00:23:40,300
<i>Kenken and his gang
hatch another evil scheme.</i>

318
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:43,730
<i>In exchange for telling
him who can fix his leg...</i>

319
00:23:43,754 --> 00:23:45,400
<i>...they tell him to break the embankment.</i>

320
00:23:46,439 --> 00:23:49,760
<i>Suspecting nothing, Mokku is tricked
into throwing stones at the embankment.</i>

321
00:23:51,230 --> 00:23:53,980
<i>And that night, heavy
rain begins to fall...</i>

322
00:23:54,234 --> 00:23:57,800
<i>...and an overflowing torrent of water
violently assaults the embankment.</i>

323
00:23:58,984 --> 00:24:01,400
<i>Look forward to next week's
Kashi no Ki Mokku!</i>

